                    The Recruiting Specialist position exists to review resumes and conduct phone-screens for professional and specialty positions for U.S.-based organizations. The selected candidate must have proven experience reviewing resumes against position requirements, conducting structured phone screens, and assessing whether candidates possess the required skills and depth of experience. Strong prior experience supporting U.S. recruitment is required; this is not an entry-level or grow-into-the-role opportunity. You must be able to move between different positions, ask effective follow-up questions, exercise sound judgment, and provide clear recommendations that the recruiting team can rely on.



Schedule: Monday – Friday 9:00am – 3:30pm EST





Responsibilities

• Review inbound applications and resumes against position requirements to identify candidates for phone screening;

• Conduct up to six structured phone or Zoom screens each day;

• Complete screening notes and an advance-or-decline recommendation immediately after each conversation and before beginning the next screen; and

• Maintain accurate candidate updates and use designated time and open screening blocks for additional resume review and sourcing.





Qualifications

• Proven experience reviewing resumes and conducting phone screens for U.S.-based professional and specialty positions;

• Demonstrated ability to assess whether a candidate’s experience and skills align with position requirements;

• Strong interviewing, listening, probing, and follow-up skills;

• Excellent spoken and written English;

• Sound judgment and the ability to make clear, well-supported candidate recommendations;

• Ability to prepare accurate, detailed, and decision-ready screening notes;

• Experience managing multiple positions and screening priorities;

• Reliable attendance and availability to work the required U.S. Eastern Time schedule; and

• Reliable internet service and a quiet, professional workspace for candidate calls.



